  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "NM02110",
    "sub_id": "51800",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>Typically use weighted systems, combining coursework, exams, and participation to calculate a 0&ndash;100% final mark, often with 50-60% as a minimum pass. Grading often includes a 5-point scale (A-F) or a 0&ndash;4.0 Grade Point Average (GPA) system. Rubrics define performance, while conduct scores may adjust final results.</div>\n",
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "1. This course is in response to the school's new project: digital learning 16+2 special teaching, some courses will be taught online and self-study online, and the student's learning status will be adjusted during the teaching period. \n2. Students who are habitually late, leave midway, or leave early are not allowed to take this course. If students fail to arrive at the roll call without special reasons, they will be deemed to have not arrived at the three quarters. Please refer to the scoring principles for the roll score rules. \n3. Absence of 12 classes (excluding special reasons) according to the regulations of the department means failing. \n4. Course progress or regulations will be slightly modified due to some unexpected factors, and students will be notified before the modification.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "1. Due to the coherent learning content of this course, in order to prevent students with bad attitudes from affecting other students, regular roll call will be implemented. If there is no special reason to miss more than 12 classes, an early warning will be notified. \n2. Students who are added, please be sure to attend the class in the first week. Course descriptions will only be given once in the first week. Students of compulsory courses should not be absent in the first week. \n3. This course will practically operate digital information content. It is recommended that students who have a laptop computer can take it with them for backup. \n4. This course has homework every week, please do not miss any homework.",
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>1.The course materials are publicly available and all content is for academic teaching only.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;2.The homework submitted for this course is open to the students in the class and can be inquired and read in iLearn.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;3.You can refer to all materials for assignments and projects, but you cannot copy the practical content of other students or</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; any copyrighted materials.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
